## **7. Performance & Scalability**
### **7.1 Latency Requirements**
| **Operation**               | **Max Latency** | **Notes**                                  |
|-----------------------------|-----------------|--------------------------------------------|
| EAW Trigger Check            | < 100 ms        | Simple threshold evaluation.              |
| EAP Assembly                 | < 2 s           | Template rendering + data assembly.       |
| Decision Timer Start         | < 500 ms        | Redis set operation.                       |
| Commander Action Handling    | < 500 ms        | Pre-authenticated commands.                |
| Command Routing              | < 1 s           | REST/gRPC API calls.                       |
| **End-to-End (WA → EAP → Commander Decision)** | **< 5 s** | Critical path. |

### **7.2 Scalability**
- **EAW Pods:**
  - **Stateless** (horizontally scalable via Kubernetes).
  - **Throughput:** 1000 WAs/sec (tested with Locust).
- **Databases:**
  - **Redis:** For **low-latency timers** (in-memory).
  - **PostgreSQL:** For **EAP/ROP storage** (relational).
  - **Kafka:** For **retaliatory queue** (ordered, persistent).
- **Caching:**
  - **Redis** for **active EAPs** and **timers**.
  - **CDN** for **static EAP templates**.

