## **1. Overview of Household Transition Engine (HTE)**
### **1.1 Purpose**
The **Household Transition Engine (HTE)** automates the generation and enforcement of **transition plans** for households flagged by the **Household Concentration Risk & Diversification System (HCRDS)**. It ensures that families **gradually adapt** to broader placement norms while maintaining child stability. For **resistant households**, it escalates to **counseling and housing-reassignment workflows**.

### **1.2 Key Objectives**
| **Goal** | **Technical Implementation** |
|----------|-----------------------------|
| **Automated Transition Plans** | Generate **customized plans** covering placement schedules, caregiver rotation, contact windows, and messaging templates. |
| **Participation Monitoring** | Track **adherence** to transition plans via checkpoints and real-time data. |
| **Escalation for Resistance** | Route **non-compliant households** to counseling and housing-reassignment workflows. |
| **Coordinator Oversight** | Enable **caseworkers** to review and adjust plans via **coordinator-reviewed templates**. |
| **Seamless Reassignment** | Integrate with **housing and scheduling systems** for smooth transitions. |

